"Druware" below means Druware Software Designs.

This software is available under two licences. You choose which one you take it
under; you do not need both, and you do not need permission to choose.


1. GNU General Public License, version 3
----------------------------------------

Free of charge, for any use, including commercial use.

The full text is in the file LICENSE, in this directory. It is the licence that
applies unless you have signed a commercial agreement with Druware.

What it asks of you, in outline — LICENSE is what actually binds:

  * If you distribute this software, or a work derived from it, you must make
    the corresponding source available to the people you distribute it to,
    under the GPLv3.
  * "Derived from" includes linking your own code against IssuesKit or against
    the application assemblies, and shipping the result.
  * You must keep the copyright notices and this licensing information intact,
    and state what you changed.
  * There is no warranty.

Running the software, modifying it for your own use, and using it inside your
organisation are not distribution, and trigger none of the above.


2. Commercial licence
---------------------

For distributing this software, or a work derived from it, without the source
disclosure the GPLv3 requires — for example, embedding IssuesKit in a closed
source product.

Terms are negotiated per agreement. Contact:

    dru@druware.com


What is covered
---------------

Everything in this repository authored by Druware, including:

    apps/Apple/      the macOS and iOS application and IssuesKit
    apps/Windows/    the Windows application and IssuesKit

The `.issues` file format itself is a data format, not software. Documents you
create with these applications are yours, and nothing here places any condition
on them.


Third-party components
----------------------

This software includes work by others, under their own licences. Those licences
are permissive and impose their own conditions — chiefly that their copyright
notices be reproduced — which apply to you under *either* option above.

See the file NOTICE for the list and the notices you must retain.


Contributions
-------------

Offering both options above requires Druware Software Designs to hold sufficient
rights in every part of the software. A contribution whose copyright Druware
does not hold, or has not been licensed broadly enough, cannot be offered under
the commercial licence — and its presence would prevent that option being
offered at all.

Contributions are therefore accepted only under an agreement granting Druware
the rights needed to license the contribution under both options. Raise this
before opening a pull request.


